From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 20:41:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Assert on the temporary buffer header size without an unused local

TemporaryFileHandle::ReadTemporaryBuffer() reads the block header size
of the index into a local that only D_ASSERT() uses, so in a release
build, where D_ASSERT() expands to nothing, the local is unused and
-Wunused-variable says so. The assertion reads the size from the index
itself.

Carried here until upstream takes it; not proposed upstream yet.

---
 src/duckdb/src/storage/temporary_file_manager.cpp | 3 +--
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/duckdb/src/storage/temporary_file_manager.cpp b/src/duckdb/src/storage/temporary_file_manager.cpp
index 87d6383999..bf59c69822 100644
--- a/src/duckdb/src/storage/temporary_file_manager.cpp
+++ b/src/duckdb/src/storage/temporary_file_manager.cpp
@@ -228,8 +228,7 @@ unique_ptr<FileBuffer> TemporaryFileHandle::ReadTemporaryBuffer(QueryContext con
                                                                 const TemporaryFileIndex &index_in_file,
                                                                 unique_ptr<FileBuffer> buffer) const {
 	auto block_index = index_in_file.block_index.GetIndex();
-	auto block_header_size = index_in_file.block_header_size.GetIndex();
-	D_ASSERT(buffer->GetHeaderSize() == block_header_size);
+	D_ASSERT(buffer->GetHeaderSize() == index_in_file.block_header_size.GetIndex());
 	AllocatedData compressed_buffer;
 	data_ptr_t read_buffer;
 	idx_t read_size;
